e) DO NOT touch `chief_live.py` or the live-streaming session path (`_live_session()`,
   `ChiefSession.say()`, used when `OPENAI_API_KEY` is set — the "fast lane"). That is
   a separate, stateful implementation with its own memory/remember() mechanism; there
   is no clean single-line place to thread a per-turn project hint through it without
   changing session state handling, and it is out of scope for a backend dispatch
   task. Leave a one-line comment where `_live_session()`/`session.say(...)` is called
   from `/api/say` and `/api/voice/ask/stream` noting that the live-session path does
   not yet receive the project hint (fallback path only) — do NOT invent new
   session-memory plumbing to fix this.

f) DO NOT modify `MOUTH_INSTRUCTIONS` (kept deliberately tiny) or `CHIEF_PROMPT`
   beyond what's already covered by (b)'s runtime-appended section — the mouth's job
   is still "relay verbatim", not "decide the project"; the browser-side realtime
   model reaching for the `project` tool argument (when it can tell from what Neill
   said) is the OpenAI Realtime API's own tool-calling behavior given the schema in
   (a), nothing here needs to teach it explicitly.

