237,708
Project switching is fully wired.

- New work defaults to Chief Command or uses the selected project’s own code and main line.
- Jess receives its own conventions and notes.
- Arch is refused before any working copy is created.
- Reviews and merging stay tied to the same project.
- Existing unassigned jobs retain their original behavior.
- The Work screen has a project picker, and fallback voice carries named-project context.
- No stored-data structure changes, live records, or frozen v1 code were touched.

Verification: all 13 new checks pass. The full run passes 302 checks with 1 skip when the known signed-out reviewer is represented as available; that temporary test-only shim was removed afterward. No commit was created, and the pre-existing Sol handoff files remain untouched.
